<title>USA: New York farmers reject grain marketing orders.</title>
<headline>New York farmers reject grain marketing orders.</headline>
<dateline>ALBANY, N.Y. 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York State Department of Agriculture and Markets said proposed marketing orders for corn, wheat, oats, barley and soybeans failed to receive approval from the voting producers of those five commodities.</p>
<p>A total of 581 producers cast ballots for one or more of the proposed orders prior to the close of the voting period on November 29. All five of the orders failed to meet the 51 percent affirmation majority for passage, the department said.</p>
<p>In addition, they also failed to surpass the 65 percent level required for passage on the basis of the percentage of the crop volumes marketed by those who voted.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
